# Cursor AI Rules for CAMA Pilates

## Deployment Protocol (CRITICAL)

**ALWAYS follow this exact process when making changes:**

### 1. Test Locally
```bash
npm run build  # Must succeed before committing
```

### 2. Commit Changes
```bash
git add .
git commit -m "feat(scope): description

Details...

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
```

### 3. Push & Verify
```bash
git push
# Then check: https://github.com/timottowitz/camapilates.com/actions
```

## Project Context

- **Stack**: React + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind + shadcn/ui
- **Deployment**: Cloudflare Pages (auto-deploy on push to main)
- **Build**: Deno (`deno task build`)
- **Blog**: Markdown files in `src/content/blog/*.md`

## Code Style

- TypeScript strict mode
- ESM modules only (no `require()`)
- Functional components with hooks
- Tailwind for styling
- shadcn/ui for components

## Git Rules

- Conventional commits (feat/fix/docs/refactor/etc)
- Never commit secrets
- Always include co-authorship
- Test before push

## Security

- API keys in `.env` files only
- Never commit `.env` (use `.env.example`)
- Check `.gitignore` before committing

## Image Uploads

**CRITICAL: ONLY use Convex for ALL images**

**User drops image:**
1. Ask where (hero, product, blog, feature, logo, badge)
2. Optimize (WebP, correct size)
3. Upload to Convex via script
4. Update convexAssets.ts
5. Test `npm run build`
6. Commit & push

**Sizes (ALL in Convex):**
- Hero: 1920x1080 WebP
- Product: 1000x1000 WebP
- Blog/OG: 1200x630 PNG/JPEG
- Feature: 800x600 WebP

See `IMAGE_UPLOAD_GUIDE.md`

## More Details

See `AGENTS.md`, `.clinerules`, and `IMAGE_UPLOAD_GUIDE.md` for complete documentation.
